   "text": "PREVIOUSLY LOCATED NEAR 7.4S 76.0E IS NOW LOCATED NEAR 7.1S 76.0E, APPROXIMATELY 212 NM EAST OF DIEGO GARCIA. ANIMATED ENHANCED INFRARED(EIR) SATELLITE IMAGERY AND 221514Z MHS 89GHZ MICROWAVE IMAGERY DEPICT AN ELONGATED, LINEAR BAND OF FLARING CONVECTION WITH A BROAD LOW-LEVEL CIRCULATION(LLCC). A 220441Z ASCAT-B IMAGE SHOWS AN ELONGATED CENTER WITH 20-25KT WINDS ALONG THE SOUTHERN AND NORTHERN PERIPHERY. ENVIRONMENTAL ANALYSIS REVEALS A FAVORABLE ENVIRONMENT WITH WARM SEA SURFACE TEMPERATURES (SST) OF 29-30 C, LOW TO MODERATE VERTICAL WIND SHEAR OF 15-20 KTS, AND GOOD EQUATORWARD OUTFLOW. GLOBAL MODELS ARE IN AGREEMENT THAT 98S IS FORECAST TO TRACK GENERALLY SOUTHEASTWARD TO SOUTHWARD WITH STEADY DEVELOPMENT OVER THE NEXT 24-48 HOURS. MAXIMUM SUSTAINED SURFACE WINDS ARE ESTIMATED AT 23 TO 28 KNOTS. MINIMUM SEA LEVEL PRESSURE IS ESTIMATED TO BE NEAR 1008 MB. THE POTENTIAL FOR THE DEVELOPMENT OF A SIGNIFICANT TROPICAL CYCLONE WITHIN THE NEXT 24 HOURS REMAINS MEDIUM.",
